### Problem 24

PERSEVERE Identify the box plot that corresponds to each of the following histograms.

![Box plots i, ii, and iii.](/curriculum/module-9-lesson-5/source-image-10.png)

Plot i: The left whisker is longer than the right whisker. The median is closer to the right side of the box.

Plot ii: The left and right whiskers have similar lengths. The median is near the center of the box.

Plot iii: The right whisker is longer than the left whisker. The median is closer to the left side of the box.

![Histograms A, B, and C.](/curriculum/module-9-lesson-5/source-image-11.png)

The histograms are A, B, and C from left to right.

A. The bars reach their maximum near the left. Their heights then decrease toward the right. The distribution extends farther to the right.

B. The bars rise toward the right before the final bar decreases. The distribution extends farther to the left.

C. The bars rise to a central maximum and then decrease by similar amounts. The distribution is approximately symmetric.

